from large-animal studies</article-title><source>Anesth Analg</source><year>2005</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>488</fpage><lpage>498</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16037166</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1213/01.ANE.0000177117.80058.4D</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reade</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Of mice and men (and rats): implications of species and stimulus differences for the interpretation of studies of nitric oxide in sepsis</article-title><source>Br J Anaesth</source><year>2003</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>118</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12538363</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/bja/aeg033</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dhillon</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahadevan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bandi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Zheng</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Rumbaut</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neurophils, nitric oxide, and microvascular permeability in severe sepsis</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>2005</year><volume>128</volume><fpage>1706</fpage><lpage>1712</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16162778</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1378/chest.128.3.1706</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>